stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Requested: CRM raises Customer Change Request\n(existing_customer_name, proposed_customer_name, reason)

    Requested --> Mgmt_Pending: submitted
    Mgmt_Pending --> Approved: Management Approves
    Mgmt_Pending --> Requested: Management Sends Back (remark mandatory)

    Approved --> [*]: Current customer updated, full history retained

    note right of Approved
        On approval:
        - customer_change_requests row itself becomes the
          permanent history entry: approved_customer_name,
          approved_by, approved_at are set and never edited
          again (not just an audit-log side effect)
        - transactions.customer_name updates to the approved
          name, so the Control Sheet always shows the CURRENT
          customer without a join
        - GET /transactions/:id/customer-history returns every
          row for this transaction, oldest first — a second or
          third later change is just another permanent row,
          fully navigable, nothing overwritten
    end note

    note left of Requested
        If a further Customer Change happens later, it is a
        NEW customer_change_requests row referencing the same
        transaction — the chain of who owned this transaction,
        when, and why, stays intact indefinitely.
    end note
